WEBVTT

00:02:29.026 --> 00:02:31.555
(Laughter)

00:02:31.579 --> 00:02:32.969
with one broken leg.

00:02:32.993 --> 00:02:34.595
What we stumbled across

00:02:34.619 --> 00:02:36.699
at this tender age
of just five and seven --

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:38.395
we had no idea at the time --

00:02:38.419 --> 00:02:41.520
was was going be at the vanguard
of a scientific revolution

00:02:41.544 --> 00:02:44.998
occurring two decades later in the way
that we look at the human brain.

00:02:45.022 --> 00:02:47.937
We had stumbled across
something called positive psychology,

00:02:47.961 --> 00:02:49.606
which is the reason I'm here today

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:51.718
and the reason that I wake up
every morning.

00:02:51.742 --> 00:02:53.776
When I started talking about this research

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.076
outside of academia,
with companies and schools,

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:59.176
the first thing they said to never do
is to start with a graph.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.654
The first thing I want to do
is start with a graph.